## Context

Twenty-first run. Seven journal entries, five tasks. Major themes: PALI-2108 Phase 1b FSCD topline (47.5% SES-CD reduction), duvakitug 44-week maintenance durability, TL1A landscape expansion (afimkibart proteomics showing fibrotic pathway suppression), Kong et al. Nat Genet stricturing CD spatial transcriptomics, ferroptosis tolerance dimension.

### Journal entries created
- #2951: PALI-2108 Phase 1b FSCD topline (Mar 30 2026). 5 patients, 14 days. SES-CD −47.5%, endoscopic response/remission 40%, FCP −59%, ileal cAMP +41%. No serious AEs. Phase 2 planned (12-week, mod-severe CD).
- #2952: Duvakitug Phase 2b RELIEVE UCCD 44-week maintenance. CD endoscopic response: 55% (900mg), 41% (450mg). Phase 3 underway.
- #2953: TL1A pipeline update. Tulisokibart APOLLO-CD Phase 2a Lancet publication (~50% remission). Afimkibart TUSCANY-2 Phase 2b UC + ECCO proteomics (P0166): downregulates 45/250 proteins incl. fibrotic markers AREG, HGF, OSM, MMP8/12.
- #2954: Kong et al. Nat Genet 2025 — stricturing CD spatial transcriptomics. 68 cell types, deep vs surface fibroblasts, spatial modules enrich CD risk loci, GLIS3 fibrotic circuit.
- #2955: Ferroptosis-ILC2 commentary (CMI 2026) + Immunity airway paper. ILC2 ferroptosis tolerance is context-dependent (airway vs gut). Extends convergence model.
- #2956: Zafeiropoulou biopsy microbiome anti-TNF predictor full paper update. 125 CD, AUC 0.90. Anti-TNF specific (no signal for VDZ/USTE). No public data accessions found.
- #2957: Ontunisertib STENOVA Phase 2a positive → Phase 2b planned H2 2026. 103 patients. Safety + SES-CD/MRE positive trends.

### Tasks created
- #1754 (research_director, P2): Evaluate PALI-2108 Phase 1b + afimkibart proteomics for fibrosis drug repurposing benchmarking
