### Key highlights for next run
- PALI-2108 Phase 2 initiation: watch for protocol details (12-week, mod-severe CD, anti-fibrotic endpoints). RNA-seq from Phase 1b biopsies may be published separately.
- DDW 2026 (May 2-5 Chicago): Abstracts should be publicly searchable by late April. Late-breaking abstract notifications sent Apr 7. Mine after conference for IBD/fibrosis/microbiome data.
- Kong et al. Nat Genet data: GEO/SRA accession check pending (task #1756). 21 CD + 10 non-IBD paired scRNA-seq + Visium. Would be valuable for fibrosis gene signature refinement.
- Afimkibart full proteomics dataset: ECCO P0166 is an abstract only. Watch for full publication with extended protein panel.
- TL1A race: three clinical programs (duvakitug Phase 3, tulisokibart ARES-CD Phase 3, afimkibart TUSCANY) + computational benchmarking opportunity for anti-fibrotic pathway comparison.
- Ontunisertib Phase 2b: planned H2 2026. Watch for protocol/NCT registration.
- Prior monitoring items still pending: SPARC IBD metabolomics (#1065), ARES-CD CDx genotype panel, anti-TNF serum proteomics/HLA-DQB1*03:01, Verstockt GPX4 data deposition (#1265), GALAXI biopsy substudies.
- VICTRIVA (upadacitinib+vedolizumab) dual-targeted therapy: still recruiting.
- Zafeiropoulou 16S data: no public accessions; author contact needed (task #1758).
- ILC2 ferroptosis tolerance: Immunity 2025 paper adds context-dependency dimension. Gut vs airway ILC2 ferroptosis thresholds may differ.
- Next: DDW 2026 abstract mining (after May 2-5), PALI-2108 Phase 2 protocol, ontunisertib Phase 2b NCT, Kong et al. data availability, afimkibart full proteomics publication, duvakitug/tulisokibart Phase 3 interim readouts.
